# Line endings, pinned rather than left to each machine.
#
# These trees are read by BOTH Windows git (core.autocrlf=true, checks out CRLF) and
# WSL/Linux git (native = LF). `text=auto` alone resolves "native" per-platform, so the
# same working tree looks clean to one git and shows every file modified to the other --
# all false positives, with no content change. eol=crlf makes both agree.
#
# Repo content stays LF. Working tree is CRLF on every platform. Every repo under
# IgnyteSoftware carries this policy; install.ps1 reports any that do not.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# PowerShell is only ever run on Windows. Explicit even though the blanket rule covers it.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.psd1 text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they fail to execute.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Never commit a symlink into these repos. Git for Windows defaults core.symlinks=false,
# which turns a committed symlink into a text file containing a path.
